Now I see the key issue! Look at line 3130-3131:

```c
/* Save the length of the array */
size_t *p = (size_t*) dst - 1;
*p = length;
```

This writes the array length to `*(size_t*)(dst - 1)`. This is the `arrayLength` field of the Variant struct, which is located just before the `data` pointer in memory.

